-- ind-c-tests-ambiguous: assertions that do not hold against the encoding where ind-c judges the SOURCE ambiguous.  Each states the reading ind-c
-- would have taken, which the encoding does not take or does not offer.  Expected count: 8 failed and 4 refused (a refusal is the encoding declining
-- to answer where this reading gives a value; it is reported at Warning severity, which is that finding and no other warning).
-- Rows marked PRE-COMMITTED were registered as amb(A|B) in expectations.md before the encoding was opened; rows marked POST-HOC were added afterwards.

§ `fixtures`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Office of the Minister`
`ind-c Minister on` d MEANS `Endnotes: the office of the Minister on` d `the favoured interpretation`

GIVEN firstDay IS A DATE
      expires IS A DATE
      reappointed IS A BOOLEAN
      before IS A LIST OF `Period of service under the Schedules`
GIVETH AN `Appointment of the Commissioner`
`ind-c Commissioner term` firstDay expires reappointed before MEANS
    `Appointment of the Commissioner` WITH
        `the day of the appointment` IS firstDay
        `the first day of the term` IS firstDay
        `the day the term expires` IS expires
        `the person appears to the Minister to be suitable` IS TRUE
        `the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission were sought on` IS NOTHING
        `a notice of intention was presented to the States on` IS NOTHING
        `the person was serving as the Commissioner on the day of the appointment` IS FALSE
        `the term is followed by a re-appointment` IS reappointed
        `the day on which the person became a member of the States` IS NOTHING
        `the service before this appointment` IS before

GIVEN from IS A DATE
      stopped IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Period of service under the Schedules`
`ind-c service` from stopped MEANS
    `Period of service under the Schedules` WITH `first day of service` IS from, `day service stopped` IS stopped, `as a designated relevant person` IS FALSE

`ind-c education entity` MEANS
    Entity WITH
        name IS "Ind-C Test Entity"
        `standing on the register` IS `entered in the general section`
        `kinds of entity` IS LIST `a company`
        `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE
        governors IS EMPTY
        purposes IS LIST (Purpose WITH description IS "education", head IS JUST `the advancement of education`, `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS FALSE, `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS FALSE, `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS FALSE)

§ `vintages before the first consolidated text (V-08, S1.2-04b PRE-COMMITTED; the (ba) and Comptroller rows POST-HOC)`

-- Reading A: before 1 January 2019 the text of these definitions is known from the instruments that later changed them, because the endnotes list every amendment:
-- R&O.40/2019 Schedule 2 paragraph 1(e) shows the words of the Minister definition that it replaced; L.13/2019 Schedule 3 paragraph 1 shows the Law the Comptroller definition named;
-- R&O.56/2025 Article 1 and L.1/2017 Article 30(3) INSERT (ba) and the Dormant Bank Accounts words; endnotes [1], [2] and [5] (src:931-943) list no earlier amender.
-- Reading B (the brief's rule, and the encoding's): no consolidated version before 1 January 2019 is among the sources, so the answer is a refusal.  All four rows REFUSE.
#ASSERT `ind-c Minister on` (YMD 2017 6 1) EQUALS `the Chief Minister`
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: the Dormant Bank Accounts words are in the text of` `before the first consolidated version`
#ASSERT NOT `Endnotes: Article 2(1)(ba) is in force on` (YMD 2018 6 1) `the favoured interpretation`
#ASSERT `Endnotes: the enactment that defines the Comptroller on` (YMD 2018 6 1) `the favoured interpretation` EQUALS `the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961`

§ `month and year ends (S1.1-13, S1.3-01, S2.2-01 PRE-COMMITTED)`

-- src:762 | (5) When appointing a person as the Commissioner the Minister must determine the period of the appointment, being not more than 6 years.
-- S1.1-13, reading B (C-MONTH ROLLOVER): six years from 29 February 2024 run to 1 March 2030, so a term expiring on 1 March 2030 is not more than 6 years.
-- The encoding offers no rollover reading of the 6 years (F9.2 is about what the end date denotes; both its readings clamp with `add years`).
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is within the limit` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c Commissioner term` (YMD 2024 2 29) (YMD 2030 3 1) FALSE EMPTY)
-- src:780 | (a) he or she resigns from office by giving not less than 3 months’ notice in writing to the Minister;
-- S1.3-01, reading B (C-NOTICE, clear months): notice given 15 January 2026 for 15 April 2026 is too short.  No reading of F9.3 counts clear months.
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(1)(a) the day the office ends by resignation` `the favoured interpretation` (`Notice of resignation of the Commissioner` WITH `the day the notice was given` IS YMD 2026 1 15, `the notice is in writing and given to the Minister` IS TRUE, `the day the resignation takes effect` IS YMD 2026 4 15) EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:826 | (a) he or she resigns from office by giving not less than one month’s notice in writing to the Minister;
-- S2.2-01, reading B (C-NOTICE, clear months): notice given 15 March 2026 for 15 April 2026 is too short.
#ASSERT `Sch 2 para 2(1)(a) the day the position ends by resignation` `the favoured interpretation` (`Notice of resignation of a member of the tribunal` WITH `the day the notice was given` IS YMD 2026 3 15, `the notice is in writing and given to the Minister` IS TRUE, `the day the resignation takes effect` IS YMD 2026 4 15) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `twelve years in aggregate (S1.3-11b POST-HOC)`

-- src:792 | (c) the person completes 12 years (whether consecutive or in aggregate) of service as Commissioner.
-- Reading: service in whole-year stretches adds by calendar length, so 6 years (1 March 2014 to 1 March 2020) and 6 years from 1 March 2022 complete 12 years on 1 March 2028,
-- and 6 years (1 March 2013 to 1 March 2019) and 6 years from 1 March 2021 complete them on 1 March 2027.  The encoding (F9.6 A) counts the DAYS of 12 calendar years from the earliest
-- first day of service, so where the stretches straddle a different number of 29 Februaries than the 12 years from that day, the expiry moves a day: 29 February 2028 (a day early)
-- and 2 March 2027 (a day late).  Neither reading of F9.6 adds the stretches' calendar lengths.
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 3(4) the appointment has expired by the day` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c Commissioner term` (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2028 3 1) TRUE (LIST (`ind-c service` (YMD 2014 3 1) (YMD 2020 3 1)))) (YMD 2028 2 29)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(4) the appointment has expired by the day` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c Commissioner term` (YMD 2021 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 1) TRUE (LIST (`ind-c service` (YMD 2013 3 1) (YMD 2019 3 1)))) (YMD 2027 3 1)

§ `public benefit determined by someone 7(1) does not name (A7-01b POST-HOC)`

-- src:203 | (1) Paragraphs (2) and (3) apply to the Commissioner, the tribunal and the court when determining the question of whether an entity provides or intends to provide public benefit, for the purpose of Article 5(1)(b).
-- src:212 | (b) treat one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons as being a section of the public, and accordingly must not treat an entity that benefits only such a person or persons as providing public benefit.
-- Reading: public benefit (Article 5(1)(b)) cannot be benefit to one identified natural person whoever asks the question; 7(3)(b) says what follows from the meaning of
-- the public.  Other reading (the encoding's): 7(3)(b) binds only the bodies 7(1) names, so another determiner's finding stands.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `ind-c education entity` (`Determination of public benefit` WITH `who made the determination` IS `any person`, `the determination finds that the entity provides public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS TRUE, `the determination finds that the entity intends to provide public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS FALSE, `regard was had to the guidance published under Article 5(4)` IS TRUE, `regard was had to how benefit gained or likely to be gained by members of the entity or other persons (other than as members of the public), and disbenefit incurred or likely to be incurred by the public, compare with the benefit gained or likely to be gained by the public` IS TRUE, `benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only` IS FALSE, `regard was had to whether any condition on obtaining the benefit, including any charge or fee, is unduly restrictive` IS TRUE, `a particular charitable purpose was presumed to be for the public benefit` IS FALSE, `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons` IS TRUE, `one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons was treated as a section of the public` IS FALSE)

§ `a disclosure to the Commissioner (A31-01 PRE-COMMITTED, reading B)`

-- src:677 | (a) by or on behalf of the Commissioner, for purpose of enabling the Commissioner to discharge any of his or her functions;
-- Reading B: a governor who passes information to the Commissioner so that the Commissioner can discharge a function is within 31(a), so no offence.  Reading A (ind-c's
-- default, and the encoding's): 31(a) needs a disclosure by or on behalf of the Commissioner, so without consent it is an offence.  The encoding has no reading B.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 29(1) the person commits an offence` `ind-c G8 A` FALSE (`Information received and its character` WITH `relates to the business or other affairs of a person` IS TRUE, `received under or for the purposes of this Law` IS TRUE, `received directly or indirectly from a person who so received it` IS FALSE, `already made available to the public from other sources` IS FALSE, `in the form of a summary or collection that identifies no particular person` IS FALSE) (`Disclosure of information` WITH `by or on behalf of the Commissioner` IS FALSE, `recipient` IS `a disclosure to any other person`, `to enable the Commissioner to discharge a function` IS TRUE, `to enable the recipient to discharge a function` IS FALSE, `to enable the recipient to discharge a function in relation to charities` IS FALSE, `for the investigation or prosecution of an offence` IS FALSE, `for taking or deciding whether to take proceedings under this Law` IS FALSE, `in circumstances prescribed by Regulations` IS FALSE, `required by the recipient for its functions` IS FALSE, `consent of the person to whom the information relates` IS FALSE, `consent of the person from whom the information was received` IS FALSE)

§ `consequential amendment of Article 6(5) under Article 39(2) (A39-06 PRE-COMMITTED, reading B)`

-- src:737 | (2) A power under this Law to amend, by Regulations, any provision of this Law includes the power to make such transitional, consequential, incidental or supplementary amendments to any other provision of this Law as appears to the States to be necessary or expedient.
-- src:200 | (b) to alter the effect of paragraph (5).
-- Reading B: 39(2) gives the power of 6(3) the power to make consequential amendments of other provisions, 6(5) included.  Reading A (ind-c's default, and the
-- encoding's): the specific limit of 6(4)(b) prevails.  The encoding offers no reading B.
#ASSERT `Art 6(4) the Regulations are within the power of Article 6(3)` (`Content of Regulations under Article 6(3)` WITH `adds sub-paragraphs to paragraph (1)` IS TRUE, `adds sub-paragraphs to paragraph (2)` IS FALSE, `the sub-paragraphs added to paragraph (2) make explanatory provision in relation to sub-paragraphs added to paragraph (1)` IS FALSE, `amends or restricts the effect of any of paragraphs (1)(a) to (p) and (2)(a) to (f)` IS FALSE, `alters the effect of paragraph (5)` IS TRUE)
